name britannica-1911-articles
# Encyclopaedia Britannica, 11th Edition (1911). An article is its headword, in capitals, and its paragraphs. What an
# article attests of its headword is the articles it refers to ("see CATACOMB", "See BIBLIOGRAPHY AND BIBLIOLOGY").
# The text of the article is its content, a usage of the headword, not a claim keyed by its whole text.
match britannica-1911-*.txt
format britannica

thing article headword
# A reference is "See"/"see" and the headword it names: parted so that only the name is said.
part crossref by | is space
content headword lead text other See see
value - See see
attest article crossref
